<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Cabot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1450–c. 1500</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Giovanni Caboto</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Cabot, born Giovanni Caboto in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, was a navigator who sailed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bristol">Bristol</a> under a patent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-vii-of-england">Henry VII of England</a>. In 1497 he reached the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>, probably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> or Cape Breton, the first European known to do so since the Norse. He set out on a second voyage in 1498 and is believed to have been lost at sea.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-cabot.jpg" alt="John Cabot" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giustino Menescardi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JohnCabotPainting.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
